  "details": "- CVE-2026-106585: a compressed packet could inflate far beyond the maximum\n  packet size and exhaust memory; reject it once the decompressed payload\n  reaches PACKET_MAX_SIZE. Backport upstream commit e0f85d83.\n- CVE-2026-106555: sshd kept GSSAPI client state from a partially completed\n  authentication attempt and could reuse it in a later attempt; reset it before\n  each attempt. Backport upstream commits 670510d1 and d549f99d.\n- CVE-2026-106553: sshd stored delegated GSSAPI credentials even when GSSAPI\n  user authorization had not succeeded; store them only after it succeeds.\n  Backport upstream commit 6f9cd19a.\n- CVE-2026-106583: ssh(1) accepted '$' and '\\' in a command-line user name,\n  allowing injection via shell-expanded commands; reject both characters.\n  Backport upstream commit 0c4c9a7b.",
